# Core §10 (`LANGUAGE-EXTENSION-POLICY`/`RESERVED-PREFIX-ENFORCEMENT`) — THE RESERVED `x-` PREFIX IN A TIMING `signal` LINE.
#
# The lane-mode half of `909-errors-reserved-x-prefix`. A `signal` line is
# split in lane mode, because a lane may hold `=`, so an unregistered `k=v`
# stays positional. Until this release an `x-` option key there therefore got
# `unexpected argument "x-k=1"`, the text a stray word gets, instead of the
# RESERVED diagnostic every other option-key position gives. Lines 14 and 15
# pin that diagnostic; line 16 pins that an ordinary unknown key keeps the
# surplus-argument text.
figdown 0.5 block
timing w "W"
signal clk p...
signal a 01
signal b 01 x-vendor-key=1
signal c 0=1 data=q x-vendor-key=2
signal d 01 bogus=1
